#: includes/class-empedia-plugin.php
msgid "EMPEDIA Shield protects this site locally (sign-in protection, file check, firewall, backups). Without a connection to EMPEDIAcloud nothing is sent to the plugin author. The firewall stores only counters per rule and day and a few samples without IP addresses; sign-in protection stores failed-attempt counters and, with the optional second factor, the factors of each user in the site database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-empedia-plugin.php
msgid "If you connect the site to EMPEDIAcloud (urbanstudio GmbH, Germany, https://empedia.cloud), the plugin sends a technical inventory: WordPress, PHP and database versions, the list of plugins and themes with versions, security settings, file check results (paths and rule names, no file contents) and the number of administrators. It does not send names, e-mail addresses or content. EMPEDIAcloud also reaches the public site to check availability and to scan it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-empedia-plugin.php
msgid "Optional services: bot protection (EMPEDIAcaptcha) sends the check token and, with the content check, the text of a form entry and the visitor IP address to the configured service address; backups can be stored on your own storage target or at EMPEDIAcloud backup storage (encrypted on this site before they leave it). Please describe the services you switch on, and name the bot protection service in the section about forms and comments."
msgstr ""

